# GMS's own figures: 365+8x% twice on six enemies, and a dark shuriken that
# attacks six times for 9+3*floor(x/6)% once every five seconds, hitting an
# ordinary monster for 200% more. The provocation goes -- nothing here can be
# taunted -- but what the provoked enemies pay stays: GMS's ceil(x/6)% covers
# EXP and Item Drop Rate alike, and both are granted permanently, walked as a
# line.
#
# The shuriken is a side strike rather than a summon on purpose: it has to go
# out with this swing and no other, or a Night Lord holding Quad Star at a boss
# would be firing it the whole time. Its six enemies are stated rather than
# taken from the swing, because GMS's Showdown - Spread widens the talisman and
# leaves the shuriken at six.
#
# Six of them go out, and each hunts ONE enemy down -- `mobCount` is 1 in the
# client. So it scatters: against six monsters they take one apiece, and
# against a lone boss all six land on it, the second and every later one
# keeping half of itself. GMS states that cut in so many words.
name: "Showdown"
description:
  "Attacks enemies and provokes them. Provoked enemies grant more EXP. When "
  "the talisman explodes, it creates a dark shuriken, which then pursues and "
  "attacks nearby enemies."
kind: SKILL_KIND_ATTACK
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_NIGHT_LORD skill_order: 2 }
max_level: 30
required_equip_type: EQUIP_TYPE_CLAW
exceeds_master_level: true
base_delay_ms: 660
max_enemies: 6
lines: 2
base {
  skill_pct: 3.73
  exp_pct: 0.0065
  item_drop_pct: 0.0065
}
per_level {
  skill_pct: 0.08
  exp_pct: 0.0015
  item_drop_pct: 0.0015
}
side_strike {
  label: "Shuriken"
  max_enemies: 6
  lines: 6
  cooldown_seconds: 5.0
  base {
    skill_pct: 0.095
    normal_pct: 2.00
  }
  per_level { skill_pct: 0.005 }
  scatter {
    hits: 6
    repeat_final_dmg_pct: -0.50
  }
}
